# L §4.4 (tally 2.1.8 R13, X1): windows each is the plain line read again with the unknown day its answer carries,
# the first its reads met, so a window the result never reads is never taken. pay lands on one of three days at the
# end of each of ten months. January's lowest balance reads January's window only: three days taken, each 410.00 PLN,
# one plain line (lo). The balance on 2026-01-31 is a value on the plain line (510.00 PLN), so nothing is taken
# (b). 2.1.7's refcore took every window the walk met, 3^10 = 59 049 combinations, and ran for minutes.
# tally 2.2 (2.2-9): `low` and `next` are cut; the text is respelled as the `min` and the `first` they meant (L §5.14.1).
=== m.tally
model ten
  tally 2
  on 2025-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-10-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2025-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input amt: money PLN
input d1: int
input d2: int

move pay[m in months]: transfers
  on window(day_of(m, d1), day_of(m, d2))
  leg cash from world to konto amount amt

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-12-01
  amt = 100.00 PLN "s"
  d1 = 26 "s"
  d2 = 28 "s"
  opening[konto] = 410.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "s"

ask lo: min(bal(konto, d) for d in 2026-01-01 .. 2026-01-31 step 1 day) windows each
ask b: bal(konto, 2026-01-31) windows each
=== expect
b: 510.00 PLN
  cut 2025-12-31
lo: 410.00 PLN
  cut 2025-12-31
